From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:29:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 122/148] fix(gastown): reconcile carried patches with the
 520e95cb baseline (gcp-fooz4)

The BASELINE upgrade f69ec02b (v0.4.0) -> 520e95cb replayed every fork
patch with conflicts resolved in place. These are the follow-up adaptations
that only showed up once the whole stack was replayed and the suites ran
against the new baseline. Each hunk names the carried patch whose behaviour
it keeps true on top of what upstream changed.

- 0016 (gcp-co9) role prompts. Upstream still restates the pour/burn fallback
  in the witness, deacon and refinery prompts, and pins those copies with
  tests (test_work_bead_resolution_discriminator_is_pinned: >=1
  CURRENT_WISP=${GC_BEAD_ID:-} per prompt; test_witness_wisp_queries_pin_include_infra:
  >=5 witness queries). Our 0016 had replaced them with pointers. Restore the
  copies, as copies of next-iteration, and keep 0016's actual fix: every bail
  drain-acks. Queries use the 0009/0033 form. tests/test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py
  learns upstream's --labels spelling (WARRANT_LABEL), which #330 made the
  create flag; keyed on --label alone both warrant detectors (0016 dedup,
  0103 gc.kind) went blind. A plural-flag fixture pins it.
- 0009/0033 (gcp-xbl, gcp-ah8h) wisp queries. Upstream #374 added a
  target-branch-missing halt to the refinery rebase step whose CURRENT_WISP
  fallback was bare (--status=in_progress --limit=1, no --include-infra).
  Give it the open,in_progress --include-infra --limit=0 form. The witness
  startup comment keeps --include-infra on the --type=molecule line.
  tests/test_wisp_molecule_queries.py skips test harnesses (they quote the
  tokens in greps) and holds the live-status facet to the three patrol roles
  it was measured on: boot's loop arrived upstream (#261) with in_progress
  resolvers that upstream pins (test_boot_patrol_burn_resolves_current_wisp),
  so boot is left as upstream wrote it.
- 0068/0069 (gcp-5ddt) witness default branch. Upstream's test pins
  STILL_ORPHANED=false exactly once, and our fail-closed arm demoted it a
  second time. Move the default-branch resolution ahead of Step 2a and fail
  closed through upstream's own RECOVERY_BLOCKED=true, which Step 2a already
  skips and escalates. The inference gate pins the $DEFAULT_BRANCH form of
  the witness content check instead of upstream's literal origin/main.
- 0083 (gcp-oz57) the Manifold step-body pin follows upstream #489 to kimi-k3.
- 0086 (gcp-mjjg) the CLAIM_DECLINED_LIVE_OWNER prose keeps the phrase the
  live-owner test pins on one line.
- 0110 (gcp-l8td.2) restart cadence. #374's halt pour continues the
  conversation, so it is stamped like every other continuing pour, and
  test_refinery_restart_cadence.sh checks one identical stamp block per
  continuing pour (six) instead of exactly one pour per step.

